<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Tuesday 115,000- USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Tuesday 115,000- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts were 115,000 head, compared with 115,000 a week ago and 110,000 a year ago, USDA reported.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were $1.00 per cwt lower than at Monday's midsession. Trade was moderate and demand light, with offerings moderate to heavy.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    53.50 -54.50	   54.50 -55.50</p>
<p>few			53.00  55.00	   54.00  56.00</p>
<p>few limited interest early  55.50		    56.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    52.50 -54.50	   53.00 -55.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    52.50 -54.50	   53.00 -55.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to 3.00 lower</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs. 41.00 -42.00	   41.00 -43.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   41.50  45.00	   42.50  45.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    44.00 -47.50	   45.00 -48.50</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 percent carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 percent lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
